// BUG: Emitter generates `const X = X;` when a continuation binding name
// matches the called event's parameter name, causing Zig to reject:
//   "local constant 'v' shadows local constant from outer scope"
//
// MINIMAL REPRO: `| out v |> echo(v: v)` — koru-side, the continuation
// binding `v` and the param `v` are in different scopes and the source
// is well-formed. The bug is purely in the Zig emission: both lower to
// the literal Zig identifier `v`, producing `const v = v;`.
//
// The punned/positional form `echo(v)` ALSO triggers the same bug — the
// emitter collapses both surface forms to the same broken Zig. That's
// extra-bad: punning is the syntax that *should* lower without the
// redundant rebind, and doesn't.
//
// ONLY WORKAROUND: rename the binding to something different from the
// param name, e.g. `| out r |> echo(v: r)`.
//
// EXPECTED: this test should print `5`. Currently it fails at backend
// compile with a Zig shadowing error.

~import "$std/io"

~event echo { v: i32 }
| out i32

~echo = out v

~echo(v: 5)
| out v |> echo(v: v)
    | out r |> std.io:print.ln("{{ r:d }}")
